{
  "schema": "qauth-vectors/1-rc.0",
  "id": "interaction/steps",
  "description": "The steps of the QAuth step grammar, Interaction API v1-rc.0, one case per step: each is the example of the Interaction API contract, and what each transport sends for it. input.step is the step as its example shows it: its name (type), params, answer, personal data, the error of a refused answer when the example shows one, and amr. It is examples[0] of the step’s JSON Schema file, published at https://docs.qauth.dev/interaction/v1-rc.0/steps/<name>.json (apps/docs-site/public/interaction/v1-rc.0/steps/ in the repository), and validates against it. input.alternatives are the other steps the engine accepts next, preferred first, each with its params. input.fipa is the FiPA round: the issuer, the new auth_session and the step names the client listed in interaction_types_supported; it lists every step, so the case shows that listing a step the FiPA endpoint does not serve changes nothing. expected.interaction is the step read’s step-grammar members on the Interaction API: step (input.step.type), error when there is one, alternatives (every input alternative’s name, in order) and params (each offered step’s params, keyed by its name). The page’s other members (csrf, client, brand, uiLocales, expiresAt) are not the grammar’s and are left out. expected.fipa is the FiPA authorization challenge endpoint’s response (ADR-017 Decision 3): for a step it serves, status 403 with error insufficient_authorization, iss, auth_session, interaction_type_required (input.step.type), qauth_interaction_types_offered (the required step, then each alternative the endpoint serves and the client listed, in order), qauth_interaction_params (keyed by those names) and qauth_interaction_error when there is an error; for a step only the Interaction API serves, status 403 with error redirect_to_web and iss. A step the FiPA endpoint cannot serve never appears in its response, and no response carries error_description or any other prose. A server computes expected from input; a client reads expected and recovers the step, its params and its error.",
  "source": "The step examples of the Interaction API v1-rc.0 contract (libs/shared/interaction-contract, issue 590) and the step grammar’s transport mappers (libs/server/step-grammar); generated by the server-step-grammar:vectors-export target.",
